title: 'cumulus-collator: emit the scheduling-signal tail as validate_block does'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The collator skips a collation whose scheduling UMP signals some runtime's `validate_block`
    would reject or rewrite: a signal that does not decode exactly, or a repeated variant. Other
    signals still pass through in the block's order, which every runtime's `validate_block`
    reproduces, including runtimes from before it re-encoded the tail.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-collator
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: minor
